'''Good-Luck Ebisu''' is a [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the 7th anniversary's [[Best of the Best (Gacha Event)|Best of the Best]] or [[NEO Best of the Best (Gacha Event)|NEO Best of the Best]]. He was added in [[Version 9.0 Update|Version 9.0]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 520
|rarity = SR
|name1 = Good-Luck Ebisu
|name2 = Bad-Luck Ebisu
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Bad-Luck Ebisu''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Essentially a walking Pandora's Box, Ebisu can be used to bring torment to almost any opponent he comes into contact with (minus enemies that have obnoxiously long range like [[Tackey]], [[Mr. Mole]], etc). With his Long Distance ability, Ebisu is able to snipe dangerous backliners like [[Angelic Sleipnir]]. However, his many abilities make him excellent against most solo bosses, notably in [[An Ancient Curse]], and cause him to absolutely dominate in most [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] stages. He can even be used to cheese [[Lifesaving Shovel]].

At first, his low chance rate of 30% seems pathetic, but when taking account of his multi-hit attack, the rate of a debuff jumps to more than 70%, which is more than adequate to keep smaller enemy hordes at bay. Do note that as he has multiple status effects, if you are in a sticky situation, he is not completely reliable for the status effects he inflicts.

Keep in mind that Ebisu is not completely infallible, as his single target, low effect uptime and long recharge time all limit his usage, so use him as support for your other [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd control units]].

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Sniper}}

