==Trivia==
*Good-Luck Ebisu is named after the Japanese god of fishermen and luck [[wikipedia:Ebisu (mythology)|Ebisu]], who is one of the seven Japanese gods of fortune. Similar to the unit's appearance, Ebisu is often depicted as a cheery dwarf-ish man with the proportions of a baby, wearing a tall hat, and carrying a rod and fish. Ebisu is often identified with Hiruko, the misconceived firstborn son of [[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanagi]] and his sister [[Izanami of Dusk (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanami]].
*The kanji on Good-Luck Ebisu's hat is 七, meaning seven.
*The kanji engraved in the hexagon that Bad-Luck Ebisu's chains are linked to is 王, meaning king.
*The number 4649 under the skull and crossbones on Bad-Luck Ebisu's rod is a ''[[wikipedia:Japanese wordplay#Goroawase|goroawase]]'' pun on the phrase ''yoroshiku'', meaning "please be kind" or "best regards".
*Good-Luck Ebisu's knockback animation is one of the few to be animated, as he shifts how he holds the staff very quickly.
*Good-Luck Ebisu is similar to [[Mimiluga (PC Uber Rare Cat)|Mimilan Pasalan]] and [[Emperor Cat (Legend Rare Cat)|Emperor Cat]], both boasting several different anti-trait abilities that each have a 30% chance to activate.
*In 2021's [[Best of the Best (Gacha Event)|Best of the Best]] event, his description had a typo stating he inflicted negative status effects on ''[[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]]'' enemies.

